  "rating": {
    "reason": "Excluding the target itself, the closest comparators are moorestech (64 overall, catalog top with verified dense 3D factory systems, co-op, and years of iteration), Ashlands (55, broadest prior scope on paper at ~94k lines and 18 quests but zero inspectable screenshots and a failing gate), Kart Royale (50, complete polished single-loop 3D racer with 70-score screenshots), and SpaceHo2 (42, single-map 2D space 4X with AI rivals but unverified presentation). Meridian Wake sits above Ashlands and Kart Royale: it has a publicly reachable playable build, three inspected coherent gameplay frames with full HUDs, and documented end-to-end systems (694 systems, 351 hulls, 735 outfits, full Free Worlds campaign with endings, mining, boarding, escorts, autosave, CI/e2e). It sits below moorestech because it is a single-day AI-generated adaptation with 0 stars, single-player only, no multiplayer/live-ops/modding evidence, and source counts alone cannot prove balance, performance at scale, or fun. Evidence gaps: no playtest beyond loading the game shell and screenshots; performance, combat balance, and late-campaign depth unverified.",
